data.content:
In .NET 10, `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2.x**, which targets OpenAPI v3.1. Here are the breaking changes and fixes:

## 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` types removed

OpenApi v2 replaces `IOpenApiAny` with `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode`:

```csharp
// Before
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

## 2. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a dictionary

It's now a structured type with explicit properties:

```csharp
// Before
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// After
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new()
    {
        Scheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
        {
            Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
        },
        Scopes = scopes // List<string>
    }
};
```

## 3. `Schema.Nullable` removed

OpenAPI v3.1 uses JSON Schema's `type` arrays instead of a separate `nullable` flag:

```csharp
// Before
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After — to make something nullable you'd add "null" to the Type flags:
// property.Value.Type = JsonSchemaType.String | JsonSchemaType.Null;
// To ensure NOT nullable, just don't include Null in Type:
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

## 4. `OpenApiReference.Type` changed

`Type` is now `ReferenceType?` → still works but the enum values may need the full qualifier `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme`.

---

## Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Scheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
            {
                Reference = new OpenApiReference
                {
                    Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme,
                    Id = "oauth2"
                }
            },
            Scopes = scopes
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

Remove the `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;` import — that namespace no longer exists in v2.
